triage: fix_game: The game plays only one trick per round. After round 1 every hand still holds 2 cards and trick_number is 1, and after round 2 deal_number is still 1, so a 12-deal game cannot fit the 12 rounds the rules imply. The tests rightly treat one round as one complete deal (deal, bid, three tricks, score), and the platform's counted repetition can express all three tricks inside one round.
step C: building the game file
step D: evaluating
triage: revise_rules: The game is built correctly, but the design has two flaws. It needs 23 steps per round, over the limit of 20. And a thoughtless policy (always bid lowest and play the first legal card) wins well over half its games, while always bidding high loses badly.
